        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does startup registration cost in Pune?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "DPIIT recognition has no government fee. Pvt Ltd incorporation govt fees Rs 1,443-7,443. Patron's complete startup package (Pvt Ltd + DPIIT + GST + PTRC/PTEC) starts from Rs 14,999. For existing entities needing only DPIIT: Rs 4,999. Section 80IAC application Rs 4,999 additionally."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does DPIIT recognition take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "DPIIT issues the Certificate of Recognition within 2-7 working days. Total for new startup (entity + DPIIT) is 10-20 working days. For existing entities, DPIIT alone takes 3-10 working days including document preparation. Innovation narrative quality determines speed."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is DPIIT recognition same as company registration?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Company registration (SPICe+/FiLLiP) creates the legal entity with RoC. DPIIT recognition is a separate certification under Startup India providing tax benefits, funding, and regulatory relaxations. You need BOTH: first incorporate, then apply for DPIIT on startupindia.gov.in."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the benefits of DPIIT recognition?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "3-year income tax exemption (Section 80IAC - applied separately), angel tax relief (Section 56), IPR concessions (50% trademark, 80% patent), GeM Startup Runway, self-certification under 9 laws, public procurement relaxation, Seed Fund (Rs 20-50 lakh), and SIDBI Fund of Funds access."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can an existing company get DPIIT recognition?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, if Pvt Ltd, LLP, or Registered Partnership Firm, less than 10 years old, turnover below Rs 100 crore, not formed by splitting, and innovation-focused. Many Hinjewadi IT companies, Kharadi product firms, and Chakan manufacturers qualify but haven't applied."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is Section 80IAC tax exemption for startups?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "3-year income tax exemption out of first 10 years for DPIIT-recognised Pvt Ltd and LLP incorporated after 1 April 2016. NOT automatic - requires separate application to DPIIT that goes before an Inter-Ministerial Board (IMB). Patron files immediately after DPIIT recognition."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the Maharashtra startup scheme MSInS?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Maharashtra State Innovation Society provides state Unique ID, seed funding Rs 15-50 lakh, incubation programmes, Maharashtra Startup Yatra, and mentoring. Separate from DPIIT recognition and provides additional state-level benefits. Patron registers with both DPIIT and MSInS."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What entity structure should I choose?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pvt Ltd preferred for angel/VC funding - equity issuance, ESOP capability, shareholder agreements. LLP for service-based startups with 2-3 partners not planning immediate VC. Proprietorships NOT eligible for DPIIT. Patron advises based on funding plans, partner composition, and industry. Quick Answers DPIIT recognition aur company registration mein kya fark hai? Company registration MCA/RoC ke saath (legal entity). DPIIT recognition Startup India portal pe alag se (benefits). Dono alag processes hain - dono zaroori hain. Section 80IAC tax exemption automatic milti hai? Nahi. DPIIT ke BAAD alag application lagani padti hai. Inter-Ministerial Board approve karta hai. Bahut se startups miss kar dete hain. Proprietorship se DPIIT recognition mil sakti hai? Nahi. Sirf Pvt Ltd, LLP, ya Registered Partnership eligible."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
