<!-- SECTION 4: WHO CAN FILE -->
<section class="content-section" id="who-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Who Needs Startup Registration in Pune?</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Tech Startup Founders (Hinjewadi, Kharadi, Baner):</strong> SaaS, AI/ML, mobile apps. Need Pvt Ltd for investor-readiness + DPIIT for Section 80IAC tax exemption and Section 56 angel tax relief.</p>
                <p><strong>Biotech/Healthtech (Venture Center, NCL Campus):</strong> R&D-intensive startups benefit from 80% patent fee concession and Seed Fund (Rs 20-50 lakh). DPIIT recognition enables government grant access.</p>
                <p><strong>EdTech/Student Entrepreneurs (SPPU, Symbiosis):</strong> University incubation programmes. DPIIT provides credibility for fundraising and government scheme participation.</p>
                <p><strong>Existing Companies < 10 Years Old:</strong> Many Hinjewadi IT companies, Kharadi product firms, and Chakan manufacturers qualify but haven't applied - losing 80IAC, GeM, and IPR concessions.</p>
                <p><strong>D2C, Fintech, Agritech, CleanTech:</strong> Maharashtra's MSInS provides additional state seed funding, mentoring, and incubation. Dual registration (DPIIT + MSInS) is most valuable.</p>

            </div>
