                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does startup registration cost in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>DPIIT recognition has no government fee. Pvt Ltd incorporation govt fees Rs 1,443-7,443. Patron's complete startup package (Pvt Ltd + DPIIT + GST + PTRC/PTEC) starts from Rs 14,999. For existing entities needing only DPIIT: Rs 4,999. Section 80IAC application Rs 4,999 additionally.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does DPIIT recognition take?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>DPIIT issues the Certificate of Recognition within 2-7 working days. Total for new startup (entity + DPIIT) is 10-20 working days. For existing entities, DPIIT alone takes 3-10 working days including document preparation. Innovation narrative quality determines speed.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is DPIIT recognition same as company registration?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Company registration (SPICe+/FiLLiP) creates the legal entity with RoC. DPIIT recognition is a separate certification under Startup India providing tax benefits, funding, and regulatory relaxations. You need BOTH: first incorporate, then apply for DPIIT on startupindia.gov.in.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What are the benefits of DPIIT recognition?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>3-year income tax exemption (Section 80IAC - applied separately), angel tax relief (Section 56), IPR concessions (50% trademark, 80% patent), GeM Startup Runway, self-certification under 9 laws, public procurement relaxation, Seed Fund (Rs 20-50 lakh), and SIDBI Fund of Funds access.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can an existing company get DPIIT recognition?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes, if Pvt Ltd, LLP, or Registered Partnership Firm, less than 10 years old, turnover below Rs 100 crore, not formed by splitting, and innovation-focused. Many Hinjewadi IT companies, Kharadi product firms, and Chakan manufacturers qualify but haven't applied.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is Section 80IAC tax exemption for startups?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>3-year income tax exemption out of first 10 years for DPIIT-recognised Pvt Ltd and LLP incorporated after 1 April 2016. NOT automatic - requires separate application to DPIIT that goes before an Inter-Ministerial Board (IMB). Patron files immediately after DPIIT recognition.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the Maharashtra startup scheme MSInS?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Maharashtra State Innovation Society provides state Unique ID, seed funding Rs 15-50 lakh, incubation programmes, Maharashtra Startup Yatra, and mentoring. Separate from DPIIT recognition and provides additional state-level benefits. Patron registers with both DPIIT and MSInS.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What entity structure should I choose?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Pvt Ltd preferred for angel/VC funding - equity issuance, ESOP capability, shareholder agreements. LLP for service-based startups with 2-3 partners not planning immediate VC. Proprietorships NOT eligible for DPIIT. Patron advises based on funding plans, partner composition, and industry.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>DPIIT recognition aur company registration mein kya fark hai?</strong> Company registration MCA/RoC ke saath (legal entity). DPIIT recognition Startup India portal pe alag se (benefits). Dono alag processes hain - dono zaroori hain.</p><p><strong>Section 80IAC tax exemption automatic milti hai?</strong> Nahi. DPIIT ke BAAD alag application lagani padti hai. Inter-Ministerial Board approve karta hai. Bahut se startups miss kar dete hain.</p><p><strong>Proprietorship se DPIIT recognition mil sakti hai?</strong> Nahi. Sirf Pvt Ltd, LLP, ya Registered Partnership eligible.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

